# Deskflow Windows Build & Deploy

## Required workflow after code changes

After any C++/CMake change that affects the product, run **build → test → migrate** before considering the task done:

```powershell
# 1. Build (imports MSVC, vcpkg, Qt)
.\build-windows.ps1

# 2. Unit tests (reconfigure with -DSKIP_BUILD_TESTS=OFF first if tests are missing)
$env:PATH = "$PWD\.qt\6.10.3\msvc2022_64\bin;$PWD\build\bin;$env:PATH"
Set-Location build\src\lib\server
..\..\..\unittests\server\SwitchDecisionTests.exe
..\..\..\unittests\server\DisplayLayoutTests.exe
Set-Location $PWD\..\..\..\..

# 3. Migrate installed Deskflow (requires Administrator)
.\migrate-windows.ps1 -Force
```

Or combine build + migrate:

```powershell
.\migrate-windows.ps1 -BuildFirst -Force
```

Preview migration without changes: `.\migrate-windows.ps1 -WhatIf`

## migrate-windows.ps1

Copies `build/bin` into `C:\Program Files\Deskflow`, backs up to `.migration-backup/`, stops/restarts the Deskflow service. Settings in `%APPDATA%\Deskflow` are preserved.

| Flag | When |
|------|------|
| `-BuildFirst` | Run `build-windows.ps1` before copying |
| `-Force` | Required on **client** machines (protocol 1.9; server should be upgraded first) |
| `-WhatIf` | Preflight only; no admin needed |
| `-NoStart` | Install but do not restart the service |
| `-SkipBackup` | Skip backup (avoid unless urgent) |

**Admin required** for real migration. If the agent shell is not elevated, launch via UAC:

```powershell
Start-Process powershell -Verb RunAs -Wait -ArgumentList `
  "-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command `"cd '$PWD'; .\migrate-windows.ps1 -Force`""
```

## Manual incremental build (agents)

**Always import MSVC before `cmake --build`.** Without `vcvars64.bat`, STL headers fail (`cstdint` missing).

```powershell
$vcvars = "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvars64.bat"
$envFile = Join-Path $env:TEMP "deskflow-vcvars.env"
cmd /c "`"$vcvars`" >nul 2>&1 && set" | Out-File $envFile -Encoding ascii
Get-Content $envFile | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '^([^=]+)=(.*)$') { Set-Item "env:$($matches[1])" $matches[2] } }
Remove-Item $envFile -Force

cmake --build build --target deskflow deskflow-core server SwitchDecisionTests DisplayLayoutTests -j 8
```

Then run `.\migrate-windows.ps1 -Force` (elevated).

## Key paths

| Artifact | Path |
|----------|------|
| GUI (built) | `build/bin/deskflow.exe` |
| GUI (installed) | `C:\Program Files\Deskflow\deskflow.exe` |
| Migration backups | `.migration-backup/<timestamp>/` |
| Qt | `.qt/6.10.3/msvc2022_64` |

## Pitfalls

- PowerShell: use `;` not `&&`.
- New `.cpp` files need CMake reconfigure (GLOB mismatch).
- `Server.h`: qualify `deskflow::server::` types; no `using namespace` in headers.
- Client migration aborts without `-Force` when server may still be on an older build.
